WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有亲历者才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.120
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:26.580
Hello.
你好。

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.120
Hello and to love's eternal glory.
大家好，愿爱永恒荣耀。

11
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:40.740
Oh, lady, we should tell people this is the first podcast that we are recording in 2022.
噢，亲爱的，我们应该告诉大家这是我们2022年录制的第一期播客。

12
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.800
The other ones you've been listening to this year we recorded before the new year.
你们今年听到的其他几期是我们年前录好的。

13
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.720
This is our first one back after our vacations.
这是我们假期归来后的第一期。

14
00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.460
We are back.
我们回来了。

15
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.780
We are semi-rested.
我们稍微休息了一下。

16
00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.760
We're also semi-back.
我们也算半回归了。

17
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.060
I am back in my closet.
我又回到了我的衣帽间里。

18
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:58.920
You are.
确实。

19
00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.840
You are in the studio.
你在录音室里。

20
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.760
Oh, guys, there are some stricter protocols here at the beginning of 2022.
噢，伙计们，2022年初这里的防疫规定更严格了一些。

21
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.660
So I let Angela have the studio.
所以我把录音室让给了安吉拉。

22
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.820
Me and Sam.
我和山姆一起。

23
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:10.560
What's up, Sam?
你好啊，山姆？

24
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.400
Hi, everybody.
大家好。

25
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.120
Aw.
噢。

26
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.180
Hey, Sam!
嘿，山姆！

27
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.900
Cassie and I are over here on Zoom.
凯西和我在Zoom这边。

28
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:16.900
Hi, ladies.
你们好，女士们。

29
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:17.620
Hi.
你好。

30
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:24.180
I will point out, you guys, Jenna, is that a ginormous plant in your podcast closet?
我要指出一点，伙计们，珍娜，你播客衣帽间里那盆植物也太大了吧？

31
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.380
It is.
确实很大。

32
00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.140
Do you notice Cassie's got a plant over her shoulder as well?
你们注意到凯西肩膀后面也有一盆植物吗？

33
00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.560
Well, I guess when you podcast from home, you need a plant.
好吧，我想在家录播客时，确实需要一盆植物。

34
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.800
That's totally a coincidence.
这纯属巧合。

35
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.780
Sam has a little Christmas tree.
山姆有一棵小圣诞树。

36
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:37.720
Damn it.
该死。

37
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.620
Lady, are you the only one without a plant?
亲爱的，你是唯一没有植物的人吗？

38
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.840
I'm plantless.
我这儿没有植物。

39
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.000
Which is so crazy because you're the plant tracker.
这太疯狂了，因为你可是植物追踪者啊。

40
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.820
I love plants, guys.
伙计们，我爱植物。

41
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.440
I guess I'm going to have to start traveling with my own plant.
我想我以后得带着自己的植物去旅行了。

42
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.420
I'm going to be that lady.
我要成为那种女士了。

43
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.800
You know how you see people that travel always with a pet?
你知道有些人旅行时总是带着宠物吧？

44
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.720
Maybe I'm going to be the lady that's like, hey, do you see that lady with the little tiny
也许我会成为那种女士，就是那种，嘿，你看到那个在飞机上抱着一盆小多肉的女士了吗？

45
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.060
succulent in her lap on the plane?
多肉植物。

46
00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:06.000
I would love to travel with you as old ladies where you just clutch a tiny succulent the
我很乐意和你一起变老，到时候我们就像那样，全程紧紧抱着一盆小多肉。

47
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.540
whole time.
全程。

48
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:07.920
That's amazing.
那太棒了。

49
00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.640
You guys, I should share with you that for Christmas, Jenna and I exchanged gifts.
伙计们，我得告诉你们，圣诞节时，珍娜和我交换了礼物。

50
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:17.520
I got her some cozy pajama pants and she got me a succulent throw pillow.
我送了她一条舒适的睡裤，她送了我一个多肉植物形状的抱枕。

51
00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:21.480
It looks like a giant succulent, but it's a cozy pillow.
它看起来像个巨大的多肉植物，但其实是个舒适的抱枕。

52
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:22.640
It really does.
确实很像。

53
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.560
I brought it home and Isabel said, mom, is that pillow a succulent?
我把它带回家，伊莎贝尔说，妈妈，那个抱枕是多肉植物吗？

54
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.580
And I was like, yes, yes, it is, Isabel.
我就说，是的，没错，伊莎贝尔，它就是。

55
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.800
Oh my God.
天哪。

56
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:32.880
You guys, Sam just brought me a plant from the lobby.
伙计们，山姆刚从大厅给我带了一株植物。

57
00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.620
Get a picture.
拍张照吧。

58
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.620
Oh, Cassie, you need to get in this picture with your plant.
噢，凯西，你得带着你的植物一起入镜。

59
00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.460
Okay, Sam, you hold up your tree.
好了，山姆，你把你的树举起来。

60
00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:42.900
Ready?
准备好了吗？

61
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:43.540
Here we go.
我们要拍了。

62
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.520
One, two, three.
一，二，三。

63
00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.720
That is amazing.
太棒了。

64
00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:52.560
Well, you know, listen, we might have some protocols that keep us apart, but we're enjoying
好吧，听着，我们可能有一些保持距离的规定，但我们正在一起享受

65
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.440
plants together.
植物带来的乐趣。

66
00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.900
You guys, that's something.
伙计们，这可真不简单。

67
00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:55.900
It's something.
确实不简单。

68
00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.740
It's huge.
这意义重大。

69
00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.000
I'll take it.
我接受。

70
00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.140
Should we get into this episode?
我们要开始聊这一集了吗？

71
00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.240
We really should, because there's a lot of fun stuff to discuss.
确实该开始了，因为有很多有趣的内容要讨论。

72
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.260
This is The Promotion.
这一集是《升职》。

73
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.740
It is season six, episode three.
这是第六季第三集。

74
00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:14.520
It is written by Jen Salata, directed by Jen Salata, and here is your summary.
由简·萨拉塔编剧，简·萨拉塔执导，以下是剧情梗概。

75
00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:21.740
Michael and Jim's managerial power struggle intensifies when David Wallace reveals that
当大卫·华莱士透露他们没有足够的资金给办公室里的每个人发放年度加薪时，

76
00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.000
they don't have enough money to give everyone in the office their yearly raises.
迈克尔和吉姆之间的管理权之争愈演愈烈。

77
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.260
So he leaves it up to the co-managers to determine who gets a raise.
所以他把决定谁能加薪的任务留给了这两位联合经理。

78
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:39.080
Meanwhile, Pam tries to get people to give her money instead of traditional wedding gifts.
与此同时，帕姆试图让大家给她钱，而不是传统的结婚礼物。

79
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.680
That storyline really cracked me up.
那条故事线真的让我笑喷了。

80
00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.200
It did me too.
我也是。

81
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:45.320
All right.
好吧。

82
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.900
Fast fact number one.
速览事实第一条。

83
00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.100
I have a location breakdown.
我有一个外景地分析。

84
00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.000
I thought you would.
我就知道你会有的。

85
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.980
You might be thinking, wait, they didn't go anywhere on location.
你可能在想，等等，他们根本没去任何外景地拍摄啊。

86
00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.000
Please tell me your location breakdown is Jim's glass cube.
请告诉我你的外景地分析就是吉姆的玻璃隔间。

87
00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.340
It is, lady.
没错，女士。

88
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:01.400
Is it really?
真的是吗？

89
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:07.610
Well, we got a bunch of fan questions, including from Tara Jade L.
嗯，我们收到了很多粉丝提问，包括来自南澳大利亚的塔拉·杰德·L。

90
00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.390
in South Australia.
的提问。

91
00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:13.330
Can we please talk about the layout of the office changing?
我们能聊聊办公室布局的变化吗？

92
00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.050
Because I don't think it's ever mentioned.
因为我觉得剧中从来没提过这件事。

93
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.410
A new office just appears for Jim to move into that was never there before.
吉姆搬进去的那间办公室就像凭空出现的一样，之前根本不存在。

94
00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.390
And from Seoul C.
还有来自台湾的索尔·C。

95
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.510
in Taiwan, what was involved in making Jim's office?
问，建造吉姆的办公室涉及了哪些工作？

96
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.270
Did they break down the wall behind Kevin's desk to make space?
他们是为了腾出空间而拆掉了凯文办公桌后面的墙吗？

97
00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.690
And Molly S.
还有来自阿肯色州的莫莉·S。

98
00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.170
from Arkansas says, how long did this process take?
问，这个过程花了多长时间？

99
00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.990
Did it slow down the shooting at all?
它有拖慢拍摄进度吗？

100
00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.530
See, lots of questions.
你看，问题多着呢。

101
00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.710
Lots of questions.
问题真不少。

102
00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.470
I'm going to have to agree with Tara Jade.
我得同意塔拉·杰德的看法。

103
00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:43.890
It's true.
确实如此。

104
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:49.230
Jim is just suddenly in a tiny glass cube in the office and no one says anything.
吉姆突然就在办公室里弄了个小玻璃隔间，居然没人说什么。

105
00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.750
No one says, where did this come from?
没人问这东西是从哪儿来的吗？

106
00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.210
I know.
我知道。

107
00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:57.730
I would have loved just one talking head where someone was like, what the hell?
我真希望至少能有一个采访镜头，有人能说句“这到底是什么鬼？”

108
00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.590
I know.
我懂。

109
00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.990
Like, you know who would have been perfect is Ryan.
你知道谁最适合说这话吗？瑞安。

110
00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.470
Ryan being like, what the hell?
瑞安肯定会说，这到底是什么鬼？

111
00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:06.470
Jim's glass box took over the whole corner of the office.
吉姆的玻璃隔间占了办公室整个角落。

112
00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:07.510
I agree.
我同意。

113
00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:13.710
Well, Jim's office was actually a pretty simple addition that was installed over the weekend.
其实吉姆的办公室只是个简单的加建部分，周末就装好了。

114
00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:21.410
Randy Cordray shared with us that this is because we were able to build all the walls in our scenery mill,
兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，这是因为我们能在布景工厂里把所有墙板都造好，

115
00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.430
which was across the street from our studio lot.
就在我们摄影棚对面。

116
00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.230
Michael Gallenberg designed them.
迈克尔·加伦伯格负责设计。

117
00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.370
They were built by our construction coordinator, Tim James.
由我们的施工协调员蒂姆·詹姆斯负责搭建。

118
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:33.230
And then the walls were installed pretty quickly.
然后墙板很快就安装到位了。

119
00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:39.930
They did arrange our shoot schedule so that we didn't shoot inside Jim's office until later in the week.
他们特意调整了拍摄计划，直到周内晚些时候才在吉姆的办公室里拍摄。

120
00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:44.770
This was mostly so that set dressing could decorate it.
主要是为了留时间给布景师进行装饰。

121
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:45.430
Right.
没错。

122
00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:51.030
I did zoom in to see if the glass walls went all the way to our fakie ceiling.
我特意放大看了看，玻璃墙是不是一直延伸到了我们的假天花板上。

123
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:51.670
And?
结果呢？

124
00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.570
And they did.
确实连上了。

125
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.150
Oh!
噢！

126
00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.730
The top part is frosted, like these frosted rectangles.
上半部分是磨砂的，像那种磨砂长方形。

127
00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.110
And then the bottom part is clear glass with blinds.
下半部分是透明玻璃，还配了百叶窗。

128
00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:01.070
Wow.
哇。

129
00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:06.110
Well, Randy mentioned that the new office was kind of right behind Creed's area.
兰迪提到，新办公室的位置正好在克里德的办公区后面。

130
00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:09.830
They didn't have to modify anything that was existing.
他们不需要改动任何现有的设施。

131
00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:10.970
It just kind of fit.
刚好就塞进去了。

132
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.290
That's what she said.
这就是她说的意思。

133
00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:18.450
There was one piece of set dressing that Randy pointed out that he says you can't see in the episode,
兰迪指出有一件布景道具，他说在剧集里根本看不见，

134
00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.770
but he absolutely loves it.
但他特别喜欢。

135
00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:23.970
He sent us a picture of it, which is Jim's diploma.
他给我们发了张照片，是吉姆的毕业证书。

136
00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.330
What's it say?
上面写了什么？

137
00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:29.590
It's just, you know, that he graduated from college.
就是写着他大学毕业了之类的。

138
00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.810
It was created by our graphics designer, Ryan Cosgrove.
这是我们的平面设计师瑞安·科斯格罗夫制作的。

139
00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:35.530
So we can post that in Office Ladies Stories.
我们可以把它发到《办公室女士》的快拍里。

140
00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:36.750
Oh, fun.
噢，真有趣。

141
00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:39.810
That was your breakdown of Jim's Cube.
这就是你对“吉姆隔间”的深度解析。

142
00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.630
Well, you know, I noticed a few things in Jim's Cube.
其实，我在吉姆的隔间里还发现了一些东西。

143
00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:43.610
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

144
00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:44.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

145
00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.690
I noticed a calendar, which seems important.
我发现了一个日历，这似乎很重要。

146
00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:50.330
But did you see the giant poster of a train?
但你看到那张巨大的火车海报了吗？

147
00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.370
Yeah.
看到了。

148
00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.750
What's that?
那是什么？

149
00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.770
And then I thought, is there a train club at Dunder Mifflin we don't know about?
我就在想，邓德·米夫林公司是不是有个我们不知道的火车俱乐部？

150
00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.730
I mean, Dwight and Toby love trains.
我是说，德怀特和托比都很喜欢火车。

151
00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.910
We learned that in the meeting.
我们在会议上学到了那个。

152
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.910
Is there a train, Finer's thing club?
有个火车俱乐部吗，费纳的那个？

153
00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.570
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

154
00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:05.570
A train club.
一个火车俱乐部。

155
00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.190
I don't know.
我不知道。

156
00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.890
These are now three people at Dunder Mifflin that clearly have a thing for trains.
现在邓德·米夫林有三个人明显对火车情有独钟了。

157
00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:10.630
I'm just saying.
